#. Campaign mission dialogue (MissionDialogs.cpp): dialog.<res|conf>.<mission>.title / <line>.speaker / <line>.text
msgid "dialog.res.1.title"
msgstr "The Return"

msgid "dialog.res.1.1.speaker"
msgstr "Commander Quispe"

msgid "dialog.res.1.1.text"
msgstr "Three months ago we left the valleys with nothing but our rifles. The Confederation called it a rout. Today we come back down the old smugglers' trail, and they still think the jungle is empty."

msgid "dialog.res.1.2.speaker"
msgstr "Colonel Mayta"

msgid "dialog.res.1.2.text"
msgstr "Scouts report a Confederation outpost by the river. Fresh concrete, two bunkers, a supply pad. They are building to stay."

msgid "dialog.res.1.3.speaker"
msgstr "Commander Quispe"

msgid "dialog.res.1.3.text"
msgstr "Then we build faster. Raise a camp on the ridge, gather the volunteers from the villages and burn that outpost before their convoy arrives. Let the valleys hear that we are home."

msgid "dialog.res.1.4.speaker"
msgstr "Colonel Mayta"

msgid "dialog.res.1.4.text"
msgstr "Understood. The flag goes up tonight."

msgid "dialog.res.2.title"
msgstr "Jungle"

msgid "dialog.res.2.1.speaker"
msgstr "Captain Paz"

msgid "dialog.res.2.1.text"
msgstr "Commander, their engineers have cut a road through the rainforest. Heavy columns are already rolling toward our camp."

msgid "dialog.res.2.2.speaker"
msgstr "Commander Quispe"

msgid "dialog.res.2.2.text"
msgstr "Good. A road through the swamp is a trap they built for themselves. Their tanks will sink to the tracks while our people move between the trees."

msgid "dialog.res.2.3.speaker"
msgstr "Captain Paz"

msgid "dialog.res.2.3.text"
msgstr "We do not have the guns to stop all of them."

msgid "dialog.res.2.4.speaker"
msgstr "Commander Quispe"

msgid "dialog.res.2.4.text"
msgstr "We do not need to stop all of them, only to outlast them. Dig in, wall the approaches, mine the clearings and hold the camp until their waves break."

msgid "dialog.res.3.title"
msgstr "Sabotage"

msgid "dialog.res.3.1.speaker"
msgstr "Colonel Mayta"

msgid "dialog.res.3.1.text"
msgstr "Our first team never reached the fuel depot. Only their radio operator got out, and she brought the guard schedule with her."

msgid "dialog.res.3.2.speaker"
msgstr "Commander Quispe"

msgid "dialog.res.3.2.text"
msgstr "Then their sacrifice bought us a door. The depot feeds every Confederation vehicle in the province. Without it their armour is scrap metal."

msgid "dialog.res.3.3.speaker"
msgstr "Engineer Benito"

msgid "dialog.res.3.3.text"
msgstr "The charges are ready, but the detonator only works at short range. Someone has to walk right up to their fence."

msgid "dialog.res.3.4.speaker"
msgstr "Commander Quispe"

msgid "dialog.res.3.4.text"
msgstr "I will lead the second team myself. Quietly through their rear, and when the depot goes up, everyone attacks."

msgid "dialog.res.4.title"
msgstr "The Gorge"

msgid "dialog.res.4.1.speaker"
msgstr "Captain Paz"

msgid "dialog.res.4.1.text"
msgstr "The fuel fire is still burning. The Confederation is pulling a relief column through the mountain gorge: trucks, tanks and a mobile command post."

msgid "dialog.res.4.2.speaker"
msgstr "Commander Quispe"

msgid "dialog.res.4.2.text"
msgstr "The gorge is narrow and they cannot turn around in it. Whoever holds the walls of that gorge decides who leaves it."

msgid "dialog.res.4.3.speaker"
msgstr "Colonel Mayta"

msgid "dialog.res.4.3.text"
msgstr "Their command post carries the maps of every garrison in Peru. If it gets through, they will know where to hit us next."

msgid "dialog.res.4.4.speaker"
msgstr "Commander Quispe"

msgid "dialog.res.4.4.text"
msgstr "Then nothing gets through. Take positions above the road and let the column come to us."

msgid "dialog.res.5.title"
msgstr "Matter of Seconds"

msgid "dialog.res.5.1.speaker"
msgstr "Captain Paz"

msgid "dialog.res.5.1.text"
msgstr "A Confederation signal station sits 50 kilometres to the northeast of the nearest garrison. Their engineers are assembling the antenna right now."

msgid "dialog.res.5.2.speaker"
msgstr "Commander Quispe"

msgid "dialog.res.5.2.text"
msgstr "Once it is up, they will call in every gunship on the continent. We strike before the first message leaves the mast."

msgid "dialog.res.5.3.speaker"
msgstr "Engineer Benito"

msgid "dialog.res.5.3.text"
msgstr "I cut their cable last night. That buys us a little time, but not much."

msgid "dialog.res.5.4.speaker"
msgstr "Commander Quispe"

msgid "dialog.res.5.4.text"
msgstr "Then every second counts. Move!"

msgid "dialog.res.6.title"
msgstr "Radio Station"

msgid "dialog.res.6.1.speaker"
msgstr "Colonel Mayta"

msgid "dialog.res.6.1.text"
msgstr "We pulled a working radio set with their cipher keys out of the station ruins. With it we could read every Confederation order."

msgid "dialog.res.6.2.speaker"
msgstr "Commander Quispe"

msgid "dialog.res.6.2.text"
msgstr "Only if it reaches our base. Captain Paz is bringing it in an armoured carrier across open ground."

msgid "dialog.res.6.3.speaker"
msgstr "Captain Paz"

msgid "dialog.res.6.3.text"
msgstr "They know what we carry. Every patrol in the region is hunting us."

msgid "dialog.res.6.4.speaker"
msgstr "Commander Quispe"

msgid "dialog.res.6.4.text"
msgstr "Then we will draw them onto us. Hold the base, Captain, and bring that radio home in one piece."

msgid "dialog.res.7.title"
msgstr "Lima"

msgid "dialog.res.7.1.speaker"
msgstr "Commander Quispe"

msgid "dialog.res.7.1.text"
msgstr "Twenty years ago the Confederation raised its flag over Lima and called it peace. Tonight we bring the war back to its doorstep."

msgid "dialog.res.7.2.speaker"
msgstr "Colonel Mayta"

msgid "dialog.res.7.2.text"
msgstr "The intercepted orders confirm it: every remaining garrison has fallen back to defend the capital."

msgid "dialog.res.7.3.speaker"
msgstr "Commander Quispe"

msgid "dialog.res.7.3.text"
msgstr "So they are all in one place. For everyone we lost in the jungle, for everyone still waiting in the villages: build, arm and take the city."

msgid "dialog.res.7.4.speaker"
msgstr "All"

msgid "dialog.res.7.4.text"
msgstr "For a free Peru!"

msgid "dialog.conf.1.title"
msgstr "Pukalpa"

msgid "dialog.conf.1.1.speaker"
msgstr "Narrator"

msgid "dialog.conf.1.1.text"
msgstr "2038. For twenty years the World Confederation has kept order on every continent. In the east of Peru, near the town of Pukalpa, that order has started to crack."

msgid "dialog.conf.1.2.speaker"
msgstr "Senator Brandt"

msgid "dialog.conf.1.2.text"
msgstr "General Hale, you were due to report an hour ago. The Senate wants this flare-up gone before the press hears about it."

msgid "dialog.conf.1.3.speaker"
msgstr "General Hale"

msgid "dialog.conf.1.3.text"
msgstr "The rains washed out the roads, Senator. We are deploying now. Without satellite cover we will have to see this jungle with our own eyes."

msgid "dialog.conf.1.4.speaker"
msgstr "General Hale"

msgid "dialog.conf.1.4.text"
msgstr "Lieutenant Kade, build the base, keep the perimeter tight and wait for the scouts. The rebels will test us before we are ready."

msgid "dialog.conf.2.title"
msgstr "Ukayali Shore"

msgid "dialog.conf.2.1.speaker"
msgstr "Lieutenant Kade"

msgid "dialog.conf.2.1.text"
msgstr "General, the scouts found a rebel camp on the Ukayali shore, 20 kilometres north of Pukalpa. Boats bring them food and fuel every night."

msgid "dialog.conf.2.2.speaker"
msgstr "General Hale"

msgid "dialog.conf.2.2.text"
msgstr "Can we cut the river off?"

msgid "dialog.conf.2.3.speaker"
msgstr "Lieutenant Kade"

msgid "dialog.conf.2.3.text"
msgstr "Not from here. The bank is solid jungle. We go straight at the camp, or we let them grow."

msgid "dialog.conf.2.4.speaker"
msgstr "General Hale"

msgid "dialog.conf.2.4.text"
msgstr "Then we go now, while they are still counting rifles. Their approaches will be mined: send the engineers first."

msgid "dialog.conf.3.title"
msgstr "Capture of Miguel"

msgid "dialog.conf.3.1.speaker"
msgstr "Operator Yara"

msgid "dialog.conf.3.1.text"
msgstr "General, prisoners from the river camp say the rebel leader is hiding at a jungle headquarters upstream."

msgid "dialog.conf.3.2.speaker"
msgstr "General Hale"

msgid "dialog.conf.3.2.text"
msgstr "Prisoners say a lot of things. It could be bait to pull us deeper into the forest."

msgid "dialog.conf.3.3.speaker"
msgstr "Senator Brandt"

msgid "dialog.conf.3.3.text"
msgstr "Bait or not, the Senate wants a name in custody. A captured leader ends a rebellion faster than a hundred battles."

msgid "dialog.conf.3.4.speaker"
msgstr "General Hale"

msgid "dialog.conf.3.4.text"
msgstr "Understood. Kade, the factory and the tech centre are yours. Heavy armour will not pass these trails: take their headquarters with what can."

msgid "dialog.conf.4.title"
msgstr "Outpost"

msgid "dialog.conf.4.1.speaker"
msgstr "Lieutenant Kade"

msgid "dialog.conf.4.1.text"
msgstr "The headquarters was empty, General. He got away by the river while we were breaking the gates."

msgid "dialog.conf.4.2.speaker"
msgstr "General Hale"

msgid "dialog.conf.4.2.text"
msgstr "Then he is running toward the mountains. Yara, raise the forward squad."

msgid "dialog.conf.4.3.speaker"
msgstr "Operator Yara"

msgid "dialog.conf.4.3.text"
msgstr "Contact for a moment... gunfire, then something about a minefield. The channel is dead."

msgid "dialog.conf.4.4.speaker"
msgstr "General Hale"

msgid "dialog.conf.4.4.text"
msgstr "So they are waiting for us at the pass. All units, battle order: wipe out that outpost and open the road."

msgid "dialog.conf.5.title"
msgstr "Meat Grinder"

msgid "dialog.conf.5.1.speaker"
msgstr "General Hale"

msgid "dialog.conf.5.1.text"
msgstr "Senator, we took the outpost on schedule. We are digging in."

msgid "dialog.conf.5.2.speaker"
msgstr "Senator Brandt"

msgid "dialog.conf.5.2.text"
msgstr "The new satellite pictures are bad, General. Rebel units from the south are converging on your position. Many more than we counted."

msgid "dialog.conf.5.3.speaker"
msgstr "General Hale"

msgid "dialog.conf.5.3.text"
msgstr "How long until reinforcements?"

msgid "dialog.conf.5.4.speaker"
msgstr "Senator Brandt"

msgid "dialog.conf.5.4.text"
msgstr "They are coming over the mountains. Hold until they arrive, whatever it costs."

msgid "dialog.conf.6.title"
msgstr "Gorge Assault"

msgid "dialog.conf.6.1.speaker"
msgstr "Senator Brandt"

msgid "dialog.conf.6.1.text"
msgstr "You held, General. The Senate has noticed. We have located the rebels' main fortress at the end of the gorge."

msgid "dialog.conf.6.2.speaker"
msgstr "Lieutenant Kade"

msgid "dialog.conf.6.2.text"
msgstr "The approaches are walled and mined. A frontal assault would cost us the whole brigade."

msgid "dialog.conf.6.3.speaker"
msgstr "General Hale"

msgid "dialog.conf.6.3.text"
msgstr "Then we will not walk in. The tech centre can give us the Grad rocket launchers: in siege mode they reach over any wall."

msgid "dialog.conf.6.4.speaker"
msgstr "General Hale"

msgid "dialog.conf.6.4.text"
msgstr "Build a solid defence first, then break the fortress from range."

msgid "dialog.conf.7.title"
msgstr "Last Stand"

msgid "dialog.conf.7.1.speaker"
msgstr "Senator Brandt"

msgid "dialog.conf.7.1.text"
msgstr "This is the hour, General. The rebels have pulled every last fighter into their final base. A reinforcement group is on its way to you."

msgid "dialog.conf.7.2.speaker"
msgstr "General Hale"

msgid "dialog.conf.7.2.text"
msgstr "We are ready, Senator. Twenty years of order are not going to end in this jungle."

msgid "dialog.conf.7.3.speaker"
msgstr "Senator Brandt"

msgid "dialog.conf.7.3.text"
msgstr "Finish it, and the main peacekeeping army will take over from you."

msgid "dialog.conf.7.4.speaker"
msgstr "General Hale"

msgid "dialog.conf.7.4.text"
msgstr "For the Confederation. All units, advance!"

